WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.200
-Our first guest tonight is
a talented actress who you know

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.534
from movies such as "Lady Bird"
and "Booksmart."

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.801
She stars as Fanny Brice in
"Funny Girl," which is playing

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:10.501
at the August Wilson Theater
on Broadway.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:11.601
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.968
our friend Beanie Feldstein,
everybody.

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:15.667
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:22.667
♪♪

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:29.667
♪♪

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:33.067
Hello, hello!
I'm so happy you're back.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.234
-I'm so happy to be back.
And thank you so much

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.067
for that really beautiful,
very important conversation.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:40.434
-I think, uh, you know, um --
Thank you.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:41.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.100
-Thank you for giving
your platform.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.200
-That's very nice of you
to say.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.634
You look so well.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.133
And I know that
you also are recovering

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.667
or you had to recover
from COVID.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:53.234
-Yes. I just had COVID and I --

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:56.200
I truly don't know how I got it,
Seth.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.567
I don't. I am the most paran--

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:01.801
Ask anyone who even walks by me
on the street.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.701
They'd say,
"That Beanie, she's paranoid."

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:06.234
[ Laughter ]
The most paranoid person.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.000
I'm in love with my mask.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.367
I'm obsessed with my mask.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.834
I'm obsessed with my boosters.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:14.434
I don't know how it happened,
but it happened. But then --

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.534
-Did you make them test you
a second time

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:19.167
when it came back positive?
You're like, "This can't be."

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.734
-Unfortunately, I knew.
-You did? Oh, wow.

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.067
-It, like, hit me.

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:25.467
And then 10 days later, I was
back doing "Funny Girl,"

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:28.834
which is a three-hour,
like, marathon for me,

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.734
so it was a real, like,
zero-to-100 experience.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:35.601
But I'm so grateful to be back
with my cast and my crew,

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:36.868
and we're just having
such a good time.

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:39.100
-And this is really, I mean,

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.300
you know,
there are some people who say,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.400
"Oh, my God, 'Funny Girl'
is a dream role" or like,

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.534
"I can't believe
I'm playing this,"

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:46.033
but this really is
a dream role for you.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:49.000
You had your third birthday.
-Third.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.267
-Your third birthday
was "Funny Girl"-themed.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.934
-Mm-hmm. Yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:57.801
It was. That's me.
[ Applause ]

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.801
And it's -- For me, it's like
I already had the po--

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.601
you know, the pose, too,
was already happening.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:05.701
-I would say, like,
of all the girls who had

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.033
a "Funny Girl"-themed party,

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.334
it must be amazing to be the one
that's doing it on Broadway.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.033
But I'm pretty sure
you're the only one.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.200
-Yes, correct.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.434
I mean, I don't know.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.734
Let me know
if they're out there.

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:17.801
But I think I'm prob--
At least the third birthday,

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:20.267
I'm probably the only one.
-Yeah, it's really amazing.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.467
And it just must be --

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:23.434
it just must be joyous
to do it every night.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.467
-It's a dream, you know.
Finally now

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.434
we're getting to interact with
people more at the stage door.

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:29.801
And we just have like mothers
bringing their daughters,

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.868
daughters bringing
their mothers, aunts.

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:35.701
It's such a warm room that we
get to enter into every night

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:38.734
and to be a part of telling
Fanny Brice's story as a --

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:41.501
as a Jewish comedian
and performer myself,

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:44.434
it's like I would not be here
if it wasn't for Fanny.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:47.200
And so to get to embody her
every night with this,

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.634
like, delicious group
of people --

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:49.868
like, Seth, they're delicious.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.334
They're delicious.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.400
They're warm.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.834
They're talented --
beyond talented.

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:56.801
The tap dancing in the show,
the --

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.133
you know, just the costumes.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:01.300
It's just a delectable
little treat.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.734
-I think that due to --
It's a weird thing.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:06.067
Like, Fanny Brice almost seems
like a fictional character.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:07.634
And I think a lot of people
don't know

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:08.767
she was a real person.

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.033
-So many people don't.

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:12.634
I mean, people think that --
some people --

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:15.267
Yeah, they don't know that
Barbra was playing a real person

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:17.200
and that I'm now
playing Fanny Brice.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:21.033
And her legacy is for any Jewish
woman that wants to be on stage.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.667
We would not have been there
if it wasn't for Fanny Brice

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:25.601
and the ceilings
that she knocked down

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:28.434
and the rooms
she pushed herself into.

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.567
She's like, "I'm a bagel
on a plate full of onion rolls,

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.400
watch me work."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.067
And it's very special
to get to embody that.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.734
-You mentioned families,
you mentioned mothers

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.000
and daughters
and daughters and mothers.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.267
Your mother, obviously,
came to opening night.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:41.767
Has she come more than once?

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:44.868
-She's the queen of
the August Wilson Theater.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.801
I think she --
I mean, people are more excited

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:49.067
to see her than me
when I walk in.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:51.167
She's like, "Hello, it's me.

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:52.767
Yes, I'm Beanie's mother.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.100
Hello."

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.667
I think she's seen it
like eight -- eight times.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.634
-That's amazing.
-Maybe nine? I don't know.

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:01.067
-You can see the audience
in this show pretty well.

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:02.267
-I can see you all.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:03.501
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.367
-I can see everybody.
-Do you like that?

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:06.901
-At first I was really scared.

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:08.400
-Yeah.
-And I didn't take it in,

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.133
I think for like all of previews
and opening.

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:13.000
But now I'm, you know --
we've been doing it

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.501
for a few months and --

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:18.067
and Fanny was so known for her
relationship to the audience.

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.834
So when I'm in the numbers
in the show

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:23.868
where she is performing,
I can really like let myself go.

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:26.567
-Does it throw you when
you have family in the audience,

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.467
when your mom's there?
Do you know where she's sitting?

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.801
-Yes. And it used to --
Again, it used to throw me.

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:32.868
And now I'm like...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.734
"Hi." Not during the emo--

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.634
In none of the emotional stuff,
I can't.

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:38.300
-Right.
-But when you know, uh --

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.567
-Well, it's about being
in the -- Yeah.

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.534
-Yeah. When she's on stage
I'm like, she's on stage.

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.000
-Yeah.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.200
You had a birthday.
Was it Friday was your birthday?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.567
-Yeah, it was, you know.

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:48.434
-Oh, well, happy birthday.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:52.167
-The day the world went away.
-Yeah, right.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:53.734
-Complicated day.
-Yeah, nobody really talked

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.434
about your birthday on Friday,
now that I think about it.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.601
-No, um...
-Yeah, I did not see a CNN

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.167
breaking news --
"Beanie's birthday."

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:01.968
-Beanie's 29, very important.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:05.567
-You also announced some pretty
cool news on Friday as well.

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:08.000
-I got engaged.
-You got engaged!

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.534
Beanie got engaged!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:13.834
-Thank you.

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:16.200
You know, I think given
what's going on

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.968
in our country right now,

00:05:18.968 --> 00:05:25.033
me marrying soon to be my wife,
Bon, Bonnie, but I call her Bon.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.767
You know, I think it's really
important for us

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:30.067
to tell our story
and to live very proudly.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:33.067
And I just love her
so much, Seth.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:34.701
She's just the best thing
to ever happen to me.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.133
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:39.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
-And I know...

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:43.200
I want to -- Because I know
that you and Bon proposed --

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.601
you each proposed to each other.

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:48.467
But Bon put the work
in to sort of surprise.

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:49.501
-Yes.

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:51.300
She said to me early on,
she was like,

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.734
"I want to propose to you."

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:54.234
And I was like, "Okay."
-Yeah.

00:05:54.234 --> 00:05:55.667
-I kind of wanted
to be proposed to.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:58.400
So I was fine with it.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.467
And so, I didn't know anything.

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:01.100
And this is when I was filming

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.801
"Impeachment:
American Crime Story."

00:06:02.801 --> 00:06:06.767
So that was, for me, it was like
1998, I was in the White House,

00:06:06.767 --> 00:06:09.000
I had no idea what was going on
in the real world.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.200
I was so focused.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.300
-Very easy to surprise
you during that time.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.667
-Like, I was like, I only exist
with bangs on, like, you know.

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:18.267
It's only happening that way
for me playing Monica Lewinsky.

00:06:18.267 --> 00:06:21.601
So I was really just entrenched
in my filming

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:25.033
and it made me completely
oblivious to everything.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:26.968
Turns out everyone in my life
was lying to me.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:28.234
Just literally
every single person

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:29.300
in my life was lying to me.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.033
-So Bon reached out
to your family?

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:33.601
-Yes. And it was magical.

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:36.367
So she sent me, she was like,
"I think you need a break.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:37.767
Why don't you go
to the beach for the day?"

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:40.434
So I went with my mom and
my brother and my best friend,

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:41.734
Ana, to the beach.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.434
And then she was like,
"After, why don't we all meet up

00:06:43.434 --> 00:06:47.467
at my parents' house
and we'll do something outside,

00:06:47.467 --> 00:06:49.901
and why don't we all get dressed
up and it'll be really fun."

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.133
I was like, "Get dressed up?"

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:54.300
Like, "It's Saturday."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.968
I work all day.
I have to wear hair.

00:06:55.968 --> 00:06:59.334
I'm like, "No." And they're
like, "Let's get dressed up."

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:02.167
And I was like,
"Okay, this is weird."

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:04.234
So we go to the beach,
and my parents' house

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:05.701
is like about 50 minutes,

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:09.367
an hour from where
we were at the beach.

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:12.400
And my mom -- I keep trying
to get her in the car

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:13.934
because we're going to be late.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:17.467
And she's like, "I-I-I think
something's wrong with me."

00:07:17.467 --> 00:07:19.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.334
"I think something's wrong
with me."

00:07:20.334 --> 00:07:22.167
And I was like, "What's wrong
with you?"

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:24.567
And she's like, "Oh, my stomach,
something's wrong with me!

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:27.033
Something's wrong with me."
And I was like, "Oh, okay."

00:07:27.033 --> 00:07:28.367
We get in the car
and she's like,

00:07:28.367 --> 00:07:30.200
literally like this
behind the wheel,

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.300
like this going five miles
an hour

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.767
on the Pacific Coast Highway.

00:07:33.767 --> 00:07:36.367
And I'm like, "What is wro--
Do you want me to drive?"

00:07:36.367 --> 00:07:37.701
Like, "I'll get you
home faster."

00:07:37.701 --> 00:07:40.400
She's like, "Oh, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.701
I'm gonna drive,
I'm gonna drive,

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:43.133
I'm gonna drive."
Then she's, literally --

00:07:43.133 --> 00:07:45.434
I was like, "Is she gonna
Maya Rudolph in 'Bridesmaids'

00:07:45.434 --> 00:07:47.968
the situation
and just, like, cross PCH

00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:49.267
and poop
in the middle of the street?"

00:07:49.267 --> 00:07:51.400
Like, I was like, "What is
happening right now?"

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.300
Because she just kept screaming
that it was going to happen.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.734
And she pulls over on the side.

00:07:56.734 --> 00:07:57.801
We finally get off the highway.

00:07:57.801 --> 00:07:59.734
She pulls over in West L.A.,

00:07:59.734 --> 00:08:02.534
runs into a random restaurant,
just takes off running.

00:08:02.534 --> 00:08:06.701
I'm like, "What is happening?"
She gets back in the car.

00:08:06.701 --> 00:08:09.400
Finally, we pull up
to my parents' house

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.701
and my nephews are standing
in the driveway

00:08:11.701 --> 00:08:13.234
and they're teenagers

00:08:13.234 --> 00:08:15.901
and they're wearing little
matching shirts.

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:17.100
And I get out of the car.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.467
I'm like,
"What are you guys doing here?"

00:08:18.467 --> 00:08:20.434
They weren't supposed to be
at the gathering

00:08:20.434 --> 00:08:21.868
and they're like,
"Hi, Aunt Beanie."

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:23.601
And they, like,
won't look me in the eye.

00:08:23.601 --> 00:08:25.100
And I'm like, "What?

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.767
What are you --
What's happening?"

00:08:26.767 --> 00:08:29.567
My youngest nephew, Charlie,
reaches into his pocket.

00:08:29.567 --> 00:08:34.033
This is when I start to cry.
And he pulls out my ring for Bon

00:08:34.033 --> 00:08:35.501
that I had gotten months ago.

00:08:35.501 --> 00:08:37.200
Because I wanted
to be prepared in case --

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.667
-Yeah.

00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:41.167
-And he goes, "I think
you're gonna need this."

00:08:41.167 --> 00:08:43.601
-Aw!
[ Audience aws ]

00:08:43.601 --> 00:08:45.734
-Can you just --
I can't handle it.

00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:46.868
And I start screaming.

00:08:46.868 --> 00:08:48.767
I'm like, "Am I getting
engaged?!"

00:08:48.767 --> 00:08:50.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.067 --> 00:08:53.000
And Bon said she could
hear it from the backyard.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.834
And I walk out.
-There we go.

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:58.267
Look at that.
Bon, well done, Bon!

00:08:58.267 --> 00:09:03.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
Very well done.

00:09:03.234 --> 00:09:05.534
-So the first thing -- so sweet.

00:09:05.534 --> 00:09:07.934
So, we literally --

00:09:07.934 --> 00:09:10.234
She proposes to me then she
doesn't know I have the ring.

00:09:10.234 --> 00:09:12.434
I propos-- I get down
on one knee, I propose back.

00:09:12.434 --> 00:09:15.000
She's so shocked, she goes,
"Uh, okay?"

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.400
[ Laughter ]
That was her response.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.234
Very loving.
And we kiss, we hug.

00:09:19.234 --> 00:09:21.300
And the first thing
as an engaged person

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.667
that I whisper in Bon's ear is,

00:09:23.667 --> 00:09:27.100
"My mom -- My mom almost pooped
on the side of the road."

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:30.801
And she goes, "It was all a lie
to make sure

00:09:30.801 --> 00:09:32.000
you didn't get here early."

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.968
And I was like,
"My mom deserves an Oscar."

00:09:34.968 --> 00:09:37.400
I was like, "This is
literally the best."

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.100
And I've worked with
some amazing people, Seth.

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.801
It was the best performance
I'd ever seen in my life.

00:09:40.801 --> 00:09:43.567
-So, wait, even pulling over
at a restaurant and running in?

00:09:43.567 --> 00:09:44.968
-Fake.
-Wow!

00:09:44.968 --> 00:09:46.467
-She's so committed.

00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:47.934
-Are you --
-And she's also, I guess,

00:09:47.934 --> 00:09:49.801
afraid of Bon, because she knew
she couldn't be here early.

00:09:49.801 --> 00:09:51.467
-Now, are you moving forward?

00:09:51.467 --> 00:09:53.467
Are you ever going to be able
to trust your mother again

00:09:53.467 --> 00:09:55.567
knowing that
she's that good a liar?

00:09:55.567 --> 00:09:56.667
-No.
-Yeah.

00:09:56.667 --> 00:09:58.267
-It's gone for me now.
-That's very --

00:09:58.267 --> 00:09:59.968
-I didn't know she had it
in her, Seth, let me tell you.

00:09:59.968 --> 00:10:03.567
-That is shocking.
-And it was extraordinary work.

00:10:03.567 --> 00:10:05.067
Extraordinary work.

00:10:05.067 --> 00:10:07.000
I was like, "I need
to take some notes."

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.434
-You mentioned Maya Rudolph.

00:10:08.434 --> 00:10:10.767
You were recently
a bridesmaid as well.

00:10:10.767 --> 00:10:14.567
And you would
argue the harder job.

00:10:14.567 --> 00:10:17.167
-Yes. Now that I'm engaged,
I'm going to be a bride --

00:10:17.167 --> 00:10:19.667
Being maid of honor
is like this weird superpower.

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:21.267
Like, that you're like,
"I'm the maid of honor."

00:10:21.267 --> 00:10:22.801
And they're like,
"Right this way."

00:10:22.801 --> 00:10:25.801
You're like,
"This is incredible."

00:10:25.801 --> 00:10:28.000
So I was the maid of honor in my
best friend Melanie's wedding.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.400
And it was at this beautiful
hotel right outside of L.A.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.033
And my parents
were also invited,

00:10:33.033 --> 00:10:34.367
and my mom calls me.

00:10:34.367 --> 00:10:37.300
I'm with Melanie, getting ready,
and she's like,

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:40.000
"You won't guess who I ran into
at the breakfast.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.534
Kristen Wiig and her family
are here.

00:10:41.534 --> 00:10:44.200
And I was like, she's my --
You know.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.267
-Yes, I know.
-No offense, Seth.

00:10:46.267 --> 00:10:49.501
-No, I'll take it.
-She is my everything.

00:10:49.501 --> 00:10:52.601
And I was like, "Oh, my God,
I can't believe this.

00:10:52.601 --> 00:10:54.133
That's insane." But I was with
the bride all day.

00:10:54.133 --> 00:10:56.400
So I, you know,
focused on that, like,

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:57.834
you know, "Tell her I said hi."

00:10:57.834 --> 00:10:59.501
-You're not allowed
even as a --

00:10:59.501 --> 00:11:01.234
As a maid of honor,
you're not allowed to be like,

00:11:01.234 --> 00:11:02.467
"I gotta bounce."

00:11:02.467 --> 00:11:03.567
-You can't leave to go see
Kristen Wiig.

00:11:03.567 --> 00:11:04.968
-"Kristen Wiig's here.
I gotta go."

00:11:04.968 --> 00:11:07.467
-You have to focus
on the bride, it's imperative.

00:11:07.467 --> 00:11:10.067
So we're lining up,
and the wedding is in the middle

00:11:10.067 --> 00:11:13.300
of the beautiful hotel,
and we're lining up.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:15.234
And I'm last before Melanie,

00:11:15.234 --> 00:11:17.234
the gorgeous bride
and my best friend.

00:11:17.234 --> 00:11:21.734
And I'm stepping out to go
literally walk down the aisle

00:11:21.734 --> 00:11:24.901
and I see Kristen and her family
and they're waiting

00:11:24.901 --> 00:11:29.234
because they don't want to run
in the middle of the ceremony.

00:11:29.234 --> 00:11:32.767
And I'm wearing my mask
and I'm like -- pull it down,

00:11:32.767 --> 00:11:34.000
I'm like [Whispering] "Kristen!

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.667
It's Beanie!"

00:11:35.667 --> 00:11:37.868
And I was like,
"I'm a bridesmaid!"

00:11:37.868 --> 00:11:39.501
And she starts laughing.

00:11:39.501 --> 00:11:40.801
I'm in a pink dress.

00:11:40.801 --> 00:11:42.434
I was like, "This is the best
moment of my life!"

00:11:42.434 --> 00:11:43.801
[ Laughter ]
"Oh, my God!"

00:11:43.801 --> 00:11:44.834
I don't think
you understand, like,

00:11:44.834 --> 00:11:46.267
we grew up on that.

00:11:46.267 --> 00:11:48.868
Like, that movie came out
my senior year of high school.

00:11:48.868 --> 00:11:51.767
It is like the reason I wanted
to be an actor.

00:11:51.767 --> 00:11:54.133
It is like my everything.

00:11:54.133 --> 00:11:56.667
And so to be wearing
a pink bridesmaid's dress,

00:11:56.667 --> 00:11:59.234
in front of Kristen Wiig,
I was like, "I'm done.

00:11:59.234 --> 00:12:00.300
I see ya.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:01.467
This will be better
than my wedding.

00:12:01.467 --> 00:12:02.767
Sorry, Bon."

00:12:02.767 --> 00:12:04.000
-I just want to say something.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.400
This keeps happening to you.

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:08.968
-Am I, like, amazing?
I'm amazing at manifesting.

00:12:08.968 --> 00:12:12.734
-Whatever outfit you wear,
you like, summon the fortune.

00:12:12.734 --> 00:12:16.400
You have a deep-cut favorite
Kristen Wiig sketch.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.133
And I have a lot
of respect for it.

00:12:18.133 --> 00:12:19.968
And your brother Jonah Hill
was in the sketch.

00:12:19.968 --> 00:12:21.400
-But it's not about him.

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.634
Let's just be clear.
-No, he's a prop.

00:12:23.634 --> 00:12:24.934
-He's a literal prop.

00:12:24.934 --> 00:12:27.667
He's being objectified,
as he should be.

00:12:27.667 --> 00:12:30.234
Kristen Wiig as Liza Minnelli.
-Yeah.

00:12:30.234 --> 00:12:31.467
-You know, I love a diva.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:31.467 --> 00:12:35.100
-Yeah, you love a diva.
-I love a diva.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.834
-I'm pretty sure there's maybe
no dialogue.

00:12:37.834 --> 00:12:39.767
There's very little dialogue
in the sketch.

00:12:39.767 --> 00:12:41.200
-Maybe three lines?
-And it's great.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.734
It's called "Liza Minnelli
turns on a lamp"?

00:12:42.734 --> 00:12:44.634
-Turns off -- Turns off a lamp?
-Turns off a lamp,

00:12:44.634 --> 00:12:47.334
you're right, yeah.
-Turns off a lamp, I think.

00:12:47.334 --> 00:12:51.267
Like, your generation of
"Saturday Night Live" was my --

00:12:51.267 --> 00:12:53.701
-They were A-listers.
That cast, they were A-listers.

00:12:53.701 --> 00:12:54.968
-And it was
when I was a teenager.

00:12:54.968 --> 00:12:57.200
So for me, it was just like
my comedy handbook.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.367
-Yeah.
-And you all --

00:12:58.367 --> 00:13:00.934
-I was very lucky
to sort of just be nearby

00:13:00.934 --> 00:13:02.434
while that was all happening.
-No, that's not --

00:13:02.434 --> 00:13:05.334
Take more credit.
-I was just sitting there,

00:13:05.334 --> 00:13:07.234
just like the first act
of our show.

00:13:07.234 --> 00:13:09.934
I just sit here.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:09.934 --> 00:13:11.434
-It's important
for you to listen.

00:13:11.434 --> 00:13:13.467
-I'm a good listener.
-You are a good listener.

00:13:13.467 --> 00:13:14.667
-That's what they say,
out of everybody

00:13:14.667 --> 00:13:15.834
in show business,
I'm the best listener.

00:13:15.834 --> 00:13:18.000
-You are a good listener.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.100
-But there's, I mean, like
the second place is so far --

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.534
Nobody's a good listener
in show business.

00:13:21.534 --> 00:13:22.868
It's very easy.

00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:24.667
I'm so happy you were here
tonight of all nights

00:13:24.667 --> 00:13:25.734
and congratulations again
on your engagement.

00:13:25.734 --> 00:13:27.901
-Thank you so much.
-You guys,

00:13:27.901 --> 00:13:30.033
that's Beanie Feldstein.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:30.033 --> 00:13:32.434
"Funny Girl" is playing
at the August Wilson Theatre.

00:13:32.434 --> 00:13:34.300
We'll be right back
with Matthew Modine.

